  "summary_en": "Finnish-language version of the EU High-Level Expert Group's Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI (April 2019). It sets out a voluntary framework: lawful, ethical and robust AI, four ethical principles, seven key requirements and an assessment list, applicable across the AI lifecycle. It contains no robot-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Trustworthy AI must be lawful, ethical and technically and socially robust.",
   "Four ethical principles: respect for human autonomy, prevention of harm, fairness, explicability.",
   "Seven requirements: human agency and oversight, technical robustness and safety, privacy and data governance, transparency, diversity and non-discrimination, societal and environmental wellbeing, accountability.",
   "Chapter III provides a non-exhaustive Trustworthy AI assessment list, piloted with stakeholders.",
   "Tensions and trade-offs between requirements must be documented, and redress mechanisms provided."
  ],
